1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,630
What do a student in China, an office worker in the UK and an astronaut in space all have in common?
中国的学生、英国的上班族和太空中的宇航员有什么共同点？

2
00:00:10,630 --> 00:00:13,560
They all eat instant noodles.
他们都吃方便面。

3
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:26,190
And they're not alone – over 100 billion servings of instant noodles are consumed globally each year, making them one of the world's most successful industrial foods.
而且不止他们——全球每年消费超过1000亿份方便面，使其成为全球最成功的工业化食品之一。

4
00:00:26,190 --> 00:00:28,240
But how did this happen?
但这一切是如何发生的呢？

5
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:35,640
Put simply, they're cheap to produce and cheap to buy, which was exactly what their creator intended.
简单来说，方便面生产成本低、售价便宜，这正是其发明者的初衷。

6
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:44,650
Momofuku Ando, a Japanese entrepreneur, spent a year perfecting the recipe just after the Second World War.
二战结束后，日本企业家安藤百福花了一年时间完善配方。

7
00:00:44,650 --> 00:00:56,780
He wanted to make something similar to traditional Japanese ramen noodles, while using the wheat flour given to Japan as food aid by the US government.
他想利用美国政府作为粮食援助提供给日本的小麦粉，制作出类似日本传统拉面的食物。

8
00:00:56,780 --> 00:01:04,140
His creation was instantly popular, playing a part in Japan's post-war economic rise.
他的发明一经推出便大受欢迎，为日本战后经济崛起贡献了一份力量。

9
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:18,700
Even in the year 2000 – according to a poll by the Fuji Research Institute – instant noodles were voted Japan's most successful invention, ahead of high-speed trains, laptops and karaoke.
即便到了2000年，据富士研究所的一项民意调查显示，方便面仍被评为日本最成功的发明，排名高于高铁、笔记本电脑和卡拉OK。

10
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:23,220
But Japanese people are not alone in their devotion to instant noodles.
并非只有日本人钟爱方便面。

11
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:37,260
According to the World's Instant Noodles Association, China, Indonesia, Vietnam and India – in that order – all consumed more instant noodles than Japan in 2021.
据世界方便面协会数据，2021年，中国、印度尼西亚、越南、印度（按此顺序）的方便面消费量均超过日本。

12
00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:45,030
Instant noodles' popularity abroad is in part due to how easy they are to adapt to local tastes.
方便面在海外走红，部分原因是它们很容易适配当地口味。

13
00:01:45,030 --> 00:01:54,530
In Thailand, for example, you can get green curry flavour, while in Mexico the noodles are garnished with lime and salsa.
例如在泰国能买到青咖喱味方便面，而在墨西哥，方便面会搭配青柠和萨尔萨辣酱食用。

14
00:01:54,530 --> 00:01:59,300
And it seems that consumers have grown to expect innovation.
消费者似乎也越来越期待产品创新。

15
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:10,910
Nissin, the food company founded by Ando, launches over 300 products yearly, just in Japan, according to employee Kasura Suzuki.
安藤百福创立的日清食品公司员工铃木香须罗表示，仅在日本，公司每年就推出300多款新产品。

16
00:02:10,910 --> 00:02:14,120
Instant noodles have their critics, too.
方便面也饱受争议。

17
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:25,690
Their rise in popularity has come at an environmental cost – they're made with palm oil, contributing to deforestation, and their packaging is plastic.
其风靡的背后付出了环境代价——生产使用棕榈油，加剧了森林砍伐，包装也为塑料材质。

18
00:02:25,690 --> 00:02:37,050
And while they are a hot, tasty and filling meal, instant noodles don't have much nutritional value, and include high levels of salt and fat.
尽管方便面热气腾腾、美味饱腹，但营养价值低，且含盐量和脂肪含量极高。

19
00:02:37,050 --> 00:02:44,610
Nevertheless, instant noodles are undoubtedly lifesavers in emergency or extreme situations.
尽管如此，在紧急或极端情况下，方便面无疑是救急的食物。

20
00:02:44,610 --> 00:02:55,760
More than 60 years after their invention, instant noodles have become the default food for anyone short on money, time, or even a kitchen.
方便面问世60多年后，已然成为所有缺钱、缺时间，甚至没有厨房的人的首选食物。
